From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: pinephone: detect VBUS on the USB-C port

PHY 0 has no VBUS detection on the PinePhone (no GPIO, no power supply),
so phy-sun4i-usb reports VBUS as always present: MUSB never ends the
session when the cable is pulled, the gadget stays "configured" and
usb0 keeps its carrier.

The AXP803 sees VBUS: use its USB power supply, as other A64 boards do.
It notifies the PHY when VBUS comes and goes.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-a64-pinephone.dtsi
@@ -710,5 +710,6 @@
 };
 
 &usbphy {
+	usb0_vbus_power-supply = <&usb_power_supply>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
